  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/crenicichla_edithae_en/",
      "html": "<p>A medium-sized (around 15 cm) pike cichlid from Paraguay. The fish received represent the form depicted as Crenicichla cf. edithae in Stawikowski &amp; Werner (2004: 140). Occasionally Crenicichla edithae is regarded as a synonym of C. lepidota.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/crenicichla_edithae_en/",
      "html": "<p>Paraguay.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/crenicichla_edithae_en/",
      "html": "<p>C. edithae was described scientifically in 1991 by Alex Ploeg for his wife Edith; without her help he would not have been able to finish his studies on Crenicichla. Alex and Edith died on 18 July 2014 when flight MH17 was shot down over Ukraine.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "references",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/crenicichla_edithae_en/",
      "html": "<p>Stawikowski, R. &amp; U. Werner (2004): Die Buntbarsche Amerikas. Band 3: Erdfresser, Hecht- und Kammbuntbarsche. Verlag Eugen Ulmer, Stuttgart.</p>"
    }
